^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-27 16:44] observe — User: CLI verbs lack muscle memory (unused); want intermediate Spw precipitation / flow caches for hot reload and patching; need explicit audit of write/preview/stream/precipitate/generate; plan to improve CLI and overhaul assumptions.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:44] observe — Existing law: hot.spw + pulse-mutate-beat.md define effect.l* ceilings; precipitates.spw defines runtime stage precipitates renderable as Spw; derived-surface only knows expanded; expand correctly generates not source-writes; mass/refresh/format/dev write without registry-level mode labels.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:44] decide — New plan cli-mode-overhaul. Free rename stance. Mode lattice: measure preview stream precipitate generate patch write cadence. Flow-cache under gen policy, share identity vocab with surface-identity (not a second beat config fork). Supersedes hygiene Appendix C muscle-memory preservation.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:44] decide — Commit order: taxonomy → full audit freeze → envelope fields → derived kinds → flow-cache → migrate writers → capabilities/plan → rename pass → ship.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:44] taste — Prefer modes carrying meaning over invent/map/analyze brand names; pulse/mutate/beat stay differentiated by ceiling even if help is rewritten.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:45] note — Hygiene-index commit 7 (plan status on spw) overlaps capabilities commit; absorb or rebase after hygiene lands.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:51] observe — Sibling plan naming-profile-convention-align owns profile-family qualification and head-noun law; CLI modes register there as mode not profile. Free rename of verbs still free; public mode names go through alignment map.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:24] revise — modes remain the effect contract, but the first executable slice now aligns with progressive disclosure: measure/preview/stream/precipitate/write must report product identity, completeness, revision, and ceiling before broad verb renaming or disk flow-cache work.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[rename_scope]: "Which sense verbs merge or rename first — invent+analyze, ls vs query, atlas vs map — once modes land?"
 ?[flow_cache_durability]: "Memory-only default, or disk under .spw/gen/flow/ from day one for multi-process HMR?"
 ?[precipitate_spw]: "Must planned bodies always be valid Spw, or allow parse:false JSON precipitates for non-round-trip IR?"
 ?[hygiene_overlap]: "Land hygiene commit 7 first, or absorb plan status into this plan commit 8?"
 ?[emit_ceiling]: "Does emit ever reach effect.l3.external, and must that be refused by default?"
}

